{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.BrunnianTripleExhaustion","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianTripleExhaustion","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mass.CarrierCrossingQuantisation","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BrunnianTripleExhaustion.minimal_carrier_bRatio_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianTripleExhaustion.minimal_carrier_bRatio_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BrunnianTripleExhaustion.lean#L224-L226","doc":"And that minimal carrier gives exactly zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BrunnianTripleExhaustion.borromean_is_the_unique_minimal_carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianTripleExhaustion.borromean_is_the_unique_minimal_carrier","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BrunnianTripleExhaustion.lean#L215-L222","doc":"**`M = 3` is forced to be the Borromean.** One clasp per pair is the only\ntriple summing to `3`, and it lands exactly on the degenerate locus `b₃ = 0` —\nagreeing with `CountChannelCarrierLocus.canonical_carriers_b3_eq_zero`, reached\nhere by exhaustion rather than by assignment. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BrunnianTripleExhaustion.gap_increases_beyond_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianTripleExhaustion.gap_increases_beyond_four","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BrunnianTripleExhaustion.lean#L203-L213","doc":"**`c ≤ 12` was never a restriction.** `b₃/b₂ = M − 3` increases with `M`, so\nevery carrier beyond `M = 4` is strictly further from the measured value than\n`M = 4` is. The exhaustion above therefore covers **every** crossing number, and\nno larger search exists to run. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BrunnianTripleExhaustion.carrier_gap_bounded_below","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianTripleExhaustion.carrier_gap_bounded_below","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BrunnianTripleExhaustion.lean#L186-L201","doc":"**And it misses by at least `532229/1483044 ≈ 0.35888` — 55.98 % of the\nmeasured value.** The bound is attained at `M = 4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BrunnianTripleExhaustion.no_carrier_reproduces_b3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianTripleExhaustion.no_carrier_reproduces_b3","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BrunnianTripleExhaustion.lean#L170-L184","doc":"**No carrier reproduces the measured `b₃`** — and the Brunnian hypothesis is\nnot even needed. `b₃/b₂ = M − 3` is an *integer* for any integer `M`, while\n`rMeasured` lies strictly between `0` and `1`, so no integer works at all. Stated\nwithout `3 ≤ M` because the proof does not use it; `brunnian_sum_ge_three` is what\nmakes the *gap* bound below sharp, not what makes this true. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BrunnianTripleExhaustion.pairDependent_weight_not_a_count","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianTripleExhaustion.pairDependent_weight_not_a_count","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BrunnianTripleExhaustion.lean#L160-L166","doc":"**It reduces to a count exactly when the weights agree.** So the integrality\nthat drives the exhaustion below is not a fact about crossings — it is the\nuniformity of `def:crossing-energy`, and it is the one ingredient of the excluded\nconjunction that is a definitional choice rather than a proved constraint. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BrunnianTripleExhaustion.pairDependentSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianTripleExhaustion.pairDependentSum","kind":"def","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BrunnianTripleExhaustion.lean#L155-L158","doc":"Total energy when the weight may depend on which component-pair the crossing\njoins: `cᵢ` crossings of weight `wᵢ`, over three pairs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BrunnianTripleExhaustion.uniform_weight_is_a_count","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianTripleExhaustion.uniform_weight_is_a_count","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BrunnianTripleExhaustion.lean#L149-L153","doc":"**A uniform weight makes the energy a COUNT.** This is the whole content of\n`μ ∝ c`: the multiplicity is the crossing number because the summand does not\ndepend on the crossing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BrunnianTripleExhaustion.uniformSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianTripleExhaustion.uniformSum","kind":"def","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BrunnianTripleExhaustion.lean#L145-L147","doc":"Total energy when every crossing carries the **same** weight `w`\n(`def:crossing-energy`: `q` for `L₊`, `−q⁻¹` for `L₋`, uniformly). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BrunnianTripleExhaustion.brunnian_sum_ge_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianTripleExhaustion.brunnian_sum_ge_three","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BrunnianTripleExhaustion.lean#L137-L141","doc":"**A Brunnian carrier links every pair**, so each `mᵢ ≥ 1` and the sum is `≥ 3`.\nThis is what makes `b₃/b₂` a *non-negative* integer rather than merely an integer. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BrunnianTripleExhaustion.bRatioOfTriple_eq_bRatio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianTripleExhaustion.bRatioOfTriple_eq_bRatio","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BrunnianTripleExhaustion.lean#L130-L135","doc":"It agrees with the crossing-count form already proved: with `c₂ = 2` and\n`c₃ = 2M`, `bRatio = M − 3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BrunnianTripleExhaustion.bRatio_depends_only_on_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianTripleExhaustion.bRatio_depends_only_on_sum","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BrunnianTripleExhaustion.lean#L122-L128","doc":"**`b₃` sees only the sum.** Two carriers whose per-pair counts differ but sum\nalike are indistinguishable — the second collapse, after\n`countChannel_depends_only_on_total`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BrunnianTripleExhaustion.bRatioOfTriple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianTripleExhaustion.bRatioOfTriple","kind":"def","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BrunnianTripleExhaustion.lean#L117-L120","doc":"`b₃/b₂` for a Brunnian `A = 3` carrier with per-pair crossing counts\n`n₊ = n₋ = mᵢ`, against the owner-ruled Hopf pair carrier `c₂ = 2`. The total\ncrossing count is `c₃ = 2(m₁+m₂+m₃)`, so this is `c₃/2 − 3`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}